<body>
<canvas id="world" aria-label="First-person game world"></canvas>
<div class="vignette" aria-hidden="true"></div><div id="fade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<main id="menu" class="screen menu">
 <div class="menu-copy"><h1>Sadman's<br><span>Parable</span></h1><p class="premise">Your story is ready.<br>Unfortunately, you weren't consulted.</p>
 <div class="menu-actions"><button id="begin" class="primary" disabled>Preparing your arrival…</button><button id="continue" hidden>Continue wandering</button><button id="menu-settings">Controls &amp; settings</button><button id="menu-endings">Things you have ended</button></div>
 <p id="discovered" class="fine">An original first-person fable.</p><p class="fine quiet">Headphones help. Obedience doesn't.</p><p class="fine quiet">Someone was here before you. The building would rather not discuss it.</p><p class="disclaimer">Unaffiliated homage to The Stanley Parable. Not affiliated with or endorsed by its creators or publishers.</p></div>
 <div class="menu-footer">A game for Sadman.<span>Local. Offline. Yours.</span></div>
</main>
<div id="hud" hidden>
 <div id="place"><span id="room-name"></span><span id="traces" hidden></span><button id="pause-small" aria-label="Pause game">Esc · Pause</button></div>
 <div id="crosshair" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div><div id="interact" hidden><span class="key">E</span><span id="interact-label"></span></div>
 <div id="subtitle" aria-live="polite"><span id="speaker">THE BUILDING</span><p id="caption"></p></div>
 <div id="hint">WASD · Walk <span>Mouse · Look</span> E · Interact <span>Esc · Pause</span></div>
 <div id="toast" role="status"></div><div id="quiet-note" hidden>You can stand up whenever you want.</div>
</div>
<section id="pause" class="screen overlay" hidden aria-labelledby="pause-title">
 <div class="panel"><h2 id="pause-title">Nothing breaks<br>when you stop.</h2><p>Your place is kept. The building can wait.</p><div class="stack"><button id="resume" class="primary">Keep wandering</button><button id="pause-settings">Controls &amp; settings</button><button id="transcript-button">What the building said</button><button id="dossier-button">What you have found</button><button id="return-room">Return to your room</button><button id="main-menu">Leave to title screen</button></div><p class="fine" id="performance"></p></div>
</section>
<section id="settings" class="screen overlay" hidden aria-labelledby="settings-title">
 <div class="panel wide"><h2 id="settings-title">You have the controls.</h2><div class="settings-columns"><div><dl><div><dt>W A S D</dt><dd>Walk</dd></div><div><dt>Mouse</dt><dd>Look around</dd></div><div><dt>E / click</dt><dd>Use the thing you're looking at</dd></div><div><dt>Shift</dt><dd>Walk impatiently</dd></div><div><dt>Esc</dt><dd>Pause / release the mouse</dd></div><div><dt>← → / ↑ ↓</dt><dd>Turn / walk, without mouse capture</dd></div><div><dt>H</dt><dd>Hide or show the room label &amp; tips</dd></div><div><dt>V / M</dt><dd>Toggle local voice / all audio</dd></div></dl></div><div class="settings-controls"><label>Mouse sensitivity<input id="sensitivity" type="range" min="0.4" max="2.4" step="0.1" value="1"><span id="sensitivity-value">1.0</span></label><label class="check"><input id="voice" type="checkbox">Local narrator voice</label><p class="fine">Uses an installed English voice only. If none is available, the captions tell the entire story.</p><label class="check"><input id="muted" type="checkbox">Mute all sound</label><label class="check"><input id="motion" type="checkbox">Reduced camera motion</label><label>Rendering detail<select id="quality"><option value="auto">Automatic</option><option value="high">High</option><option value="low">Low · quieter GPU</option></select></label><p class="fine">Your settings and discoveries stay on this machine. Nothing is sent anywhere.</p></div></div><p class="fine">Click the world to capture your mouse. If capture isn't available, drag to look or use the arrow keys. This is a desktop game, not a touch game.</p><p class="disclaimer">Sadman's Parable is an original work and an unaffiliated homage. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or approved by Crows Crows Crows, Galactic Cafe, or the creators of The Stanley Parable. It contains no dialogue, art, level layout, character, music or voice recording from that game. All writing, geometry, textures and audio here were created for this project, and the optional narration uses an installed operating-system voice rather than any actor's performance.</p><button id="settings-close" class="primary">Back</button></div>
</section>
<section id="ending" class="screen overlay ending-screen" hidden aria-labelledby="ending-title"><div class="panel ending-panel"><p id="ending-count" class="fine"></p><h2 id="ending-title"></h2><p id="ending-text"></p><p id="ending-after" class="after"></p><div class="ending-actions"><button id="again" class="primary">Begin differently</button><button id="ending-menu">Let it end here</button></div></div></section>
<section id="collection" class="screen overlay" hidden aria-labelledby="collection-title"><div class="panel wide"><h2 id="collection-title">Things you have ended.</h2><p>Only the endings you found are named here.</p><div id="ending-list"></div><button id="collection-close" class="primary">Back</button></div></section>
<section id="dossier" class="screen overlay" hidden aria-labelledby="dossier-title"><div class="panel wide"><h2 id="dossier-title">What you have found.</h2><p>Traces of whoever was here before you. The building files everything except the truth.</p><div id="dossier-list"></div><button id="dossier-close" class="primary">Back</button></div></section>
<section id="transcript" class="screen overlay" hidden aria-labelledby="transcript-title"><div class="panel wide"><h2 id="transcript-title">The building said…</h2><div id="transcript-lines"></div><button id="transcript-close" class="primary">Back</button></div></section>
<div id="error" class="screen overlay" hidden><div class="panel"><h2>Your arrival was interrupted.</h2><p id="error-text"></p><button onclick="location.reload()" class="primary">Try opening the door again</button></div></div>
